      "title": "Cheaper settings, same care",
      "narration": "A hospital bed is the most expensive place to receive care, so plans encourage alternatives. Preventive care catches problems early. Outpatient and ambulatory surgery centers handle procedures that once required admission. Home health care, skilled nursing facilities and hospice care let patients leave the hospital sooner. Urgent care centers and telehealth visits replace emergency rooms for minor problems. Plans steer members toward these settings with lower copayments and sometimes refuse to pay for inpatient care that could safely have been given elsewhere. Marcus’s outpatient knee surgery costs a fraction of an overnight stay.",
