      "title": "Utilization review",
      "narration": "Utilization management checks whether care is necessary and appropriate. Prospective review happens before care: precertification or prior authorization for a planned admission, surgery or costly drug. Concurrent review happens during care: a nurse reviewer monitors a hospital stay and approves continued days. Retrospective review happens after care, examining claims for appropriateness. Second surgical opinion programs and case management for complex conditions belong to the same family. In Maryland, utilization review decisions that deny care are adverse decisions subject to the grievance and appeal process in Lesson 27.",
